/* Interesting facts diarios (inglés A2) */
const FACTS = [{"emoji":"🦁","c1":"#f97316","c2":"#ffd166","title":"Giraffe Necks","fact":"A giraffe's neck is very long, but it has only seven neck bones — the same number as a human! Giraffes use their long necks to eat leaves at the top of tall trees. Their necks can be over two meters long. A giraffe's heart is also very big and strong. It needs a strong heart to send blood all the way up to its head. Giraffes usually sleep for less than two hours a day."},{"emoji":"🎵","c1":"#f472b6","c2":"#c084fc","title":"Piano Keys","fact":"A standard piano has 88 keys in total. There are 52 white keys and 36 black keys. Pianists use both hands to play many notes at the same time. The piano is more than 300 years old. It can play very soft sounds and very loud sounds. This is why piano music can sound so different from song to song."},{"emoji":"🚀","c1":"#7c3aed","c2":"#22d3ee","title":"Sun Size","fact":"The Sun is so big that one million Earths could fit inside it. It is the closest star to our planet. The Sun is made mostly of hydrogen and helium gas. Without the Sun's light and heat, life on Earth could not exist. Light from the Sun takes about eight minutes to reach us. The Sun also gives us energy that plants use to grow."},{"emoji":"🎬","c1":"#facc15","c2":"#f87171","title":"The First Movies","fact":"The very first movies were made in the late 1800s. They were black and white, silent, and only lasted a few seconds. There was no sound at all, only moving pictures. Piano players often performed live music in the theater to match the action. Movies slowly became longer and more detailed over time. Today, movies can be hours long with incredible sound and color."},{"emoji":"🐋","c1":"#06b6d4","c2":"#38bdf8","title":"Deepest Point","fact":"The deepest part of the ocean is called the Mariana Trench. It is located in the Pacific Ocean. The trench is deeper than Mount Everest is tall. Very few people have ever traveled to the bottom of it. The water pressure there is extremely strong. Strange and unique creatures live in this dark, cold part of the ocean."},{"emoji":"🏛️","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#b45309","title":"The Egyptian Pyramids","fact":"The pyramids of Egypt were built thousands of years ago as tombs for pharaohs. The largest pyramid is called the Great Pyramid of Giza. Workers moved huge stone blocks without the machines we have today. Some blocks weighed as much as a small car. Scientists are still studying exactly how the pyramids were built. They remain one of the most amazing structures in human history."},{"emoji":"🫀","c1":"#ec4899","c2":"#f472b6","title":"Heartbeats","fact":"Your heart beats about 100,000 times every day. It pumps blood full of oxygen to every part of your body. Your heart is a strong muscle about the size of your fist. It never stops working, even while you sleep. Exercise can help make your heart stronger. A healthy heart is important for a healthy life."},{"emoji":"🤖","c1":"#22d3ee","c2":"#6366f1","title":"How the Internet Started","fact":"The internet began as a small network used by scientists and universities. It allowed computers in different places to share information. Over time, more networks connected together, creating a much bigger system. In the 1990s, the internet became available to everyday people. Today, billions of people use the internet every single day. It has completely changed how we learn, work, and communicate."},{"emoji":"🌍","c1":"#22c55e","c2":"#4ade80","title":"Tallest Mountain","fact":"Mount Everest is the tallest mountain above sea level. It is located in the Himalayas, between Nepal and Tibet. The top of Everest is extremely cold and has very little oxygen. Many climbers try to reach the top every year. It takes weeks of preparation to climb Everest safely. The mountain is still slowly growing taller every year."},{"emoji":"🎨","c1":"#fb7185","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"The Mona Lisa","fact":"The Mona Lisa is one of the most famous paintings in the world. It was painted by the Italian artist Leonardo da Vinci. The painting shows a woman with a mysterious, gentle smile. It has hung in a museum in Paris, France, called the Louvre, for many years. Millions of visitors come to see it every year. Artists still study its techniques and colors today."},{"emoji":"💡","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"First Telephone","fact":"Alexander Graham Bell invented the telephone in 1876. Before this invention, people could only send messages by letter or telegraph. The telephone let people talk to each other from far away for the first time. Early telephones were very different from the phones we use today. Over time, telephones became smaller and easier to use. Today, most people carry a phone with them everywhere."},{"emoji":"🔢","c1":"#4ade80","c2":"#60a5fa","title":"The Invention of Zero","fact":"The number zero was a huge mathematical discovery. Ancient mathematicians in India helped develop the concept of zero that we use today. Before zero, it was much harder to write large numbers or do certain types of math. Zero allows us to have place value, like the difference between 5, 50, and 500. It might seem simple, but zero completely changed mathematics. Today, zero is used in nearly everything, from counting to computer programming."},{"emoji":"🍎","c1":"#ef4444","c2":"#f87171","title":"Honey Never Spoils","fact":"Honey can stay good to eat for thousands of years. Archaeologists have even found ancient honey that was still safe to eat. This happens because honey has very little water and is naturally acidic. These conditions make it hard for bacteria to grow. Bees make honey from the nectar of flowers. Honey has been used as food and medicine for a very long time."},{"emoji":"⛈️","c1":"#38bdf8","c2":"#7dd3fc","title":"Lightning Heat","fact":"For a moment, lightning is hotter than the surface of the Sun. This heat lasts only a tiny fraction of a second. Lightning happens during storms when electricity builds up in clouds. It can travel between clouds or from a cloud to the ground. Thunder is the sound made by the rapid heating of the air. It is important to stay safe indoors during a lightning storm."},{"emoji":"🌱","c1":"#84cc16","c2":"#a3e635","title":"Oldest Trees","fact":"Some trees are more than 4,000 years old. These ancient trees have lived through thousands of years of history. Trees grow a new ring inside their trunk every year. Scientists can count these rings to learn a tree's age. Old trees are important homes for many animals. Protecting old forests helps protect the whole environment."},{"emoji":"🦁","c1":"#f97316","c2":"#ffd166","title":"Octopus Hearts","fact":"An octopus has three hearts and blue blood. Two hearts pump blood to the gills, and one heart pumps blood to the rest of the body. Octopus blood is blue because it has copper in it, not iron like human blood. Octopuses are also very smart animals. They can open jars and solve simple puzzles. Some octopuses can even change the color and texture of their skin in less than a second."},{"emoji":"🎵","c1":"#f472b6","c2":"#c084fc","title":"Beethoven's Music","fact":"Ludwig van Beethoven was a famous composer from Germany. He kept writing beautiful music even after he lost most of his hearing. He could feel the vibrations of the piano through the floor. Many people think his later music is his best work. Beethoven wrote nine full symphonies. His music is still played by orchestras all around the world today."},{"emoji":"🚀","c1":"#7c3aed","c2":"#22d3ee","title":"Moon Walk","fact":"Twelve people have walked on the Moon. All of them were part of the American Apollo missions. The first Moon walk happened in 1969, with astronaut Neil Armstrong. The Moon has much less gravity than Earth, so astronauts could jump very high. There is no air on the Moon, so astronauts had to wear special suits. Footprints on the Moon can stay there for millions of years because there is no wind."},{"emoji":"🎬","c1":"#facc15","c2":"#f87171","title":"How Cartoons Move","fact":"Cartoons are made from thousands of individual drawings. Each drawing is slightly different from the one before it. When the drawings are shown quickly, one after another, our eyes see smooth movement. This trick is called animation. Making just one minute of classic animation could take hundreds of drawings. Today, many animated movies are made using computers instead of hand drawings."},{"emoji":"🐋","c1":"#06b6d4","c2":"#38bdf8","title":"Blue Whale","fact":"The blue whale is the biggest animal that has ever lived on Earth. It can be longer than a basketball court. A blue whale's heart alone can weigh as much as a small car. These huge animals eat tiny creatures called krill. They can eat several tons of krill every day. Blue whales are found in oceans all around the world."},{"emoji":"🏛️","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#b45309","title":"The Ancient Olympics","fact":"The first Olympic Games took place in ancient Greece almost 3,000 years ago. They were held in a city called Olympia to honor the Greek gods. Only certain events existed back then, like running and wrestling. Winners received a crown made of olive leaves instead of a medal. The modern Olympic Games were inspired by these ancient competitions. Today, athletes from all over the world compete every four years."},{"emoji":"🫀","c1":"#ec4899","c2":"#f472b6","title":"Bone Count","fact":"Babies are born with about 300 bones, but adults have only 206. Some of these bones join together as a person grows. Bones give your body its shape and help you move. They also protect important organs, like your brain and heart. Bones are stronger than you might think, but they can still break. Eating healthy food helps keep your bones strong."},{"emoji":"🤖","c1":"#22d3ee","c2":"#6366f1","title":"Robots at Work","fact":"Robots are machines that can be programmed to do tasks automatically. They are used in factories to build cars and other products quickly. Robots are also used in hospitals, space exploration, and even in some homes. Some robots can move, see, and even make simple decisions. Scientists continue to design robots that can help humans in new ways. Robots are becoming a bigger part of everyday life."},{"emoji":"🌍","c1":"#22c55e","c2":"#4ade80","title":"Biggest Desert","fact":"The biggest hot desert in the world is the Sahara, in Africa. It covers a huge part of northern Africa. Deserts are not always sandy; some have rocks or gravel instead. The Sahara can be extremely hot during the day and cold at night. Very few plants and animals can survive there. Some people have lived in the Sahara desert for thousands of years."},{"emoji":"🎨","c1":"#fb7185","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"Cave Paintings","fact":"Some of the oldest known art is found on cave walls. These paintings can be tens of thousands of years old. Early humans used natural materials, like charcoal and colored rocks, to paint animals and people. Cave paintings show us how ancient people saw their world. They are found in caves on several different continents. These artworks help scientists understand early human life."},{"emoji":"💡","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"Light Bulb","fact":"Thomas Edison helped make the electric light bulb popular. He tested many different materials before finding one that worked well. Before light bulbs, people used candles or oil lamps for light. Electric light changed how people lived and worked at night. Cities slowly began adding electric street lights. Today, light bulbs are found in almost every home in the world."},{"emoji":"🔢","c1":"#4ade80","c2":"#60a5fa","title":"The Number Pi","fact":"Pi is a special number used to work with circles. It never ends and never repeats, no matter how far you calculate it. Pi is often shortened to 3.14 for everyday math problems. It helps us find the distance around a circle and the area inside it. Mathematicians have calculated trillions of digits of pi using computers. Every year, math fans celebrate 'Pi Day' on March 14th."},{"emoji":"🍎","c1":"#ef4444","c2":"#f87171","title":"Floating Apples","fact":"Apples float in water because they are 25% air. This is a fun fact that surprises many people. Apples are also a very popular fruit around the world. They come in many colors, like red, green, and yellow. Apples are a good source of fiber and vitamins. Eating fruit like apples is an important part of a healthy diet."},{"emoji":"⛈️","c1":"#38bdf8","c2":"#7dd3fc","title":"Snowflake Shapes","fact":"No two snowflakes look exactly the same. Each one forms in a unique way as it falls through the sky. Snowflakes are made of tiny ice crystals. Most snowflakes have six sides or points. Temperature and humidity affect the shape of each snowflake. Snow can look different depending on how the flakes stick together."},{"emoji":"🌱","c1":"#84cc16","c2":"#a3e635","title":"Sunflower Movement","fact":"Young sunflowers turn to follow the Sun during the day. This movement is called heliotropism. In the morning, they face east, and by evening, they face west. As sunflowers mature, most of them stop moving and face east permanently. This helps them get more sunlight and warmth in the morning. Sunflowers are also known for their bright yellow petals."},{"emoji":"🦁","c1":"#f97316","c2":"#ffd166","title":"Sleepy Koalas","fact":"Koalas sleep for about 20 hours every day. They eat eucalyptus leaves, which do not give them much energy. This is one reason why koalas move very slowly. Eucalyptus leaves can also be a little toxic, so koalas have a special stomach to break them down safely. When koalas are awake, they spend most of their time eating. Baby koalas are called joeys, just like baby kangaroos."},{"emoji":"🎵","c1":"#f472b6","c2":"#c084fc","title":"Ancient Flutes","fact":"The oldest known musical instruments are flutes made from bone. Some of these flutes are tens of thousands of years old. Ancient people carved small holes to make different notes. This shows that humans have loved music for a very, very long time. Music was probably used for stories, dancing, and celebrations. Today, flutes are still a popular instrument in orchestras and bands."},{"emoji":"🚀","c1":"#7c3aed","c2":"#22d3ee","title":"Saturn Rings","fact":"Saturn's rings are made mostly of ice and rock. Some pieces are as small as dust, and others are as big as mountains. The rings are very wide, but actually quite thin. Saturn is the second largest planet in our solar system. It also has more than 80 known moons. Saturn is so light that it could almost float in water, if there was an ocean big enough!"},{"emoji":"🎬","c1":"#facc15","c2":"#f87171","title":"Popcorn at the Movies","fact":"Popcorn became popular at movie theaters almost 100 years ago. It was cheap to make and easy to sell during a film. The smell of popcorn became part of the whole movie experience. Today, movie theaters sell millions of bags of popcorn every year. Popcorn is also considered a whole grain snack. It has been enjoyed by movie fans for generations."},{"emoji":"🐋","c1":"#06b6d4","c2":"#38bdf8","title":"Coral Reefs","fact":"Coral reefs are home to thousands of different sea animals. They are sometimes called the 'rainforests of the sea'. Coral reefs are made by tiny living creatures called coral polyps. These reefs grow very slowly over hundreds of years. Warmer ocean water can damage and even kill coral reefs. Protecting coral reefs helps protect many other sea animals too."},{"emoji":"🏛️","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#b45309","title":"The Silk Road","fact":"The Silk Road was a huge network of trade routes connecting Asia and Europe. Traders carried silk, spices, and other goods across long distances. It also helped share ideas, art, and inventions between different cultures. The route was used for hundreds of years. Many cities grew rich and important because of this trade. The Silk Road helped connect the ancient world in amazing ways."},{"emoji":"🫀","c1":"#ec4899","c2":"#f472b6","title":"Brain Power","fact":"Your brain uses about 20% of your body's energy. This is a lot, considering the brain is a small part of your body. The brain controls almost everything you do, like thinking, moving, and feeling. It sends messages to your body through nerves. Your brain also stores memories from your whole life. Sleeping well helps your brain work better."},{"emoji":"🤖","c1":"#22d3ee","c2":"#6366f1","title":"The First Video Game","fact":"One of the first popular video games was called Pong, made in the 1970s. It was a very simple game with two paddles and a ball. Pong helped start the entire video game industry. Since then, video games have become much more advanced and detailed. Millions of people around the world play video games today. Some video games are even used to help people learn new skills."},{"emoji":"🌍","c1":"#22c55e","c2":"#4ade80","title":"Smallest Country","fact":"Vatican City is the smallest country in the world. It is located inside the city of Rome, in Italy. Even though it is small, it has its own government and flag. Vatican City is home to famous art and historic buildings. Many tourists visit it every year. Its small size makes it very different from most other countries."},{"emoji":"🎨","c1":"#fb7185","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"Vincent van Gogh","fact":"Vincent van Gogh was a famous painter known for bold colors and swirling brushstrokes. One of his most famous paintings is called The Starry Night. Van Gogh created an incredible number of paintings during his short life. His unique style became much more famous after he died. Today, his paintings are shown in museums around the world. Many artists have been inspired by his colorful, emotional style."},{"emoji":"💡","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"First Airplane","fact":"The Wright brothers flew the first airplane in 1903. Their flight lasted only a few seconds, but it changed history. Before this, many people believed humans could never fly. The Wright brothers tested many designs before their first successful flight. Airplanes today can fly much faster and farther. Air travel now connects people all around the world."},{"emoji":"🔢","c1":"#4ade80","c2":"#60a5fa","title":"The Fibonacci Sequence","fact":"The Fibonacci sequence is a pattern of numbers where each number is the sum of the two before it, like 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8. This pattern appears surprisingly often in nature. You can see it in the number of petals on some flowers or the spiral of a seashell. Sunflowers often show this pattern in their seeds. Mathematicians have studied this sequence for centuries. It shows how math and nature are closely connected."},{"emoji":"🍎","c1":"#ef4444","c2":"#f87171","title":"Banana Family","fact":"Bananas are berries, but strawberries are not. This might sound strange, but it depends on how the fruit grows. Bananas grow from a flower and have seeds inside. Strawberries actually have their seeds on the outside. Bananas are also a good source of energy and potassium. They are one of the most popular fruits in the world."},{"emoji":"⛈️","c1":"#38bdf8","c2":"#7dd3fc","title":"Rainbow Colors","fact":"A rainbow has seven main colors. They are red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, and violet. Rainbows appear when sunlight passes through raindrops in the sky. The light bends and separates into different colors. You can usually see a rainbow with the sun behind you and rain in front. Rainbows are a beautiful example of light and water working together."},{"emoji":"🌱","c1":"#84cc16","c2":"#a3e635","title":"Fast Bamboo","fact":"Bamboo can grow very fast, even one meter in a single day. It is actually a type of grass, not a tree. Bamboo is very strong and is used to build houses and furniture. It also grows in many different environments around the world. Some animals, like pandas, eat bamboo as their main food. Bamboo is considered a very sustainable plant."},{"emoji":"🦁","c1":"#f97316","c2":"#ffd166","title":"Elephant Memory","fact":"Elephants can remember other elephants for many years. They can also remember paths to water, even during a drought. Elephants live in family groups led by an older female called the matriarch. She uses her memory to guide the group to food and water. Elephants also show emotions like joy and sadness. They sometimes touch the bones of elephants that have died, almost like they are saying goodbye."},{"emoji":"🎵","c1":"#f472b6","c2":"#c084fc","title":"Big Orchestras","fact":"A full orchestra can have more than 100 musicians playing together. It includes string instruments, like violins, wind instruments, like flutes, and percussion, like drums. A person called a conductor leads the orchestra without playing an instrument. The conductor uses hand movements to keep everyone playing at the same time. Orchestras can play many types of music, from calm to exciting. Watching a live orchestra is a fun way to hear many instruments at once."},{"emoji":"🚀","c1":"#7c3aed","c2":"#22d3ee","title":"Mars Color","fact":"Mars looks red because of rust in its soil. This rust comes from iron minerals in the ground. Mars is often called the Red Planet. It has the tallest volcano in the solar system, called Olympus Mons. Scientists have sent many robots to explore Mars. They are looking for signs that water, or even life, once existed there."},{"emoji":"🎬","c1":"#facc15","c2":"#f87171","title":"Green Screens","fact":"Filmmakers use bright green or blue screens to add special effects. Actors perform in front of the screen, and computers replace the color later. This lets movies show places like outer space or ancient cities. The color green is used because it is rarely found in human skin tones. This technique is used in many movies and TV shows today. It allows filmmakers to create almost anything they can imagine."},{"emoji":"🐋","c1":"#06b6d4","c2":"#38bdf8","title":"Old Jellyfish","fact":"Jellyfish have been in the ocean for more than 500 million years. This means they lived on Earth before the dinosaurs. Jellyfish do not have a brain, a heart, or bones. Most of their body is made of water. Some jellyfish can glow in the dark. They move by pushing water out of their bodies."},{"emoji":"🏛️","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#b45309","title":"Ancient Calendars","fact":"Many ancient civilizations created their own calendars to track time. The Egyptians used the movements of the star Sirius to predict floods. The Maya created a very accurate calendar using astronomy. Calendars helped people know when to plant and harvest crops. Some ancient calendars are still studied by scientists today. They show how important timekeeping was to early societies."},{"emoji":"🫀","c1":"#ec4899","c2":"#f472b6","title":"Sneeze Speed","fact":"A sneeze can leave your body at a very high speed. Sneezing is your body's way of removing things that irritate your nose. It happens very quickly and cannot usually be stopped once it starts. Covering your mouth when you sneeze helps stop germs from spreading. Some people sneeze when they look at bright light. Sneezing is a normal and healthy reflex."},{"emoji":"🤖","c1":"#22d3ee","c2":"#6366f1","title":"Smartphones Are Powerful","fact":"A modern smartphone is more powerful than the computers used for early space missions. It can take photos, play music, and connect to the internet instantly. Smartphones combine many tools into one small device. Billions of people around the world use smartphones every day. They have changed how people communicate and find information. New features are added to smartphones every year."},{"emoji":"🌍","c1":"#22c55e","c2":"#4ade80","title":"Great Wall","fact":"The Great Wall of China is thousands of kilometers long. It was built over many centuries by different Chinese dynasties. The wall was made to protect against invasions. It goes across mountains, deserts, and grasslands. Millions of people visit the Great Wall every year. Some people believed it could be seen from space, but that is actually not true."},{"emoji":"🎨","c1":"#fb7185","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"What Is Sculpture","fact":"Sculpture is art made by shaping materials like stone, clay, wood, or metal. Sculptors can carve away material or build it up to create a form. Some sculptures are tiny, while others are as tall as buildings. Ancient civilizations created sculptures to honor gods, leaders, or important events. Sculpture is one of the oldest art forms in human history. It can be found in museums, parks, and public squares."},{"emoji":"💡","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"Printing Press","fact":"The printing press helped people share books and ideas faster. It was made popular by Johannes Gutenberg in the 1400s. Before the printing press, books had to be copied by hand. This made books expensive and rare. The printing press made it possible to make many copies quickly. This helped more people learn to read."},{"emoji":"🔢","c1":"#4ade80","c2":"#60a5fa","title":"Roman Numerals","fact":"Roman numerals are an ancient number system that uses letters instead of digits. For example, the letter V means 5, and the letter X means 10. Ancient Romans used this system for counting, trading, and building. You can still see Roman numerals today on clocks, movies, and buildings. Adding and subtracting with Roman numerals was much harder than with our modern number system. Learning Roman numerals is a fun way to explore math history."},{"emoji":"🍎","c1":"#ef4444","c2":"#f87171","title":"Chocolate Origin","fact":"Chocolate comes from the seeds of the cacao tree. These seeds are called cacao beans. Ancient civilizations in Central America were some of the first to use cacao. At first, chocolate was made into a bitter drink, not a sweet treat. Sugar was added to chocolate much later in history. Today, chocolate is enjoyed by people all around the world."},{"emoji":"⛈️","c1":"#38bdf8","c2":"#7dd3fc","title":"Hurricane Names","fact":"Hurricanes get names to make them easier to talk about. This helps people share information and warnings quickly. Hurricane names are chosen from lists made every year. Hurricanes are powerful storms that form over warm ocean water. They can cause strong winds, heavy rain, and flooding. Scientists carefully track hurricanes to help keep people safe."},{"emoji":"🌱","c1":"#84cc16","c2":"#a3e635","title":"Venus Flytrap","fact":"The Venus flytrap is a plant that eats small insects. It grows in soil that does not have many nutrients. When an insect touches tiny hairs inside the trap, it snaps shut quickly. The plant then slowly digests the insect for extra nutrients. Venus flytraps still use sunlight to grow, like other plants. They are found naturally in only a small part of the world."},{"emoji":"🦁","c1":"#f97316","c2":"#ffd166","title":"Chameleon Colors","fact":"Chameleons change color to hide or to show their feelings. They do not only change color to match their background. Bright colors can mean a chameleon is excited or angry. Chameleons also have eyes that can move in two different directions at the same time. This helps them look for food and danger at once. Their long, sticky tongues can catch insects very quickly."},{"emoji":"🎵","c1":"#f472b6","c2":"#c084fc","title":"Music and the Brain","fact":"Listening to music activates many different parts of your brain at the same time. This includes areas for emotion, memory, and movement. This is why a song can suddenly remind you of a memory. Music can also help people feel calm or full of energy. Many students listen to music while studying or exercising. Scientists are still learning new things about how music affects us."},{"emoji":"🚀","c1":"#7c3aed","c2":"#22d3ee","title":"Black Holes","fact":"A black hole's gravity is so strong that even light cannot escape. This is why we cannot see black holes directly. Black holes form when a very big star collapses. They can be millions of times heavier than our Sun. Scientists study black holes using special telescopes and math. There is a huge black hole at the center of our galaxy."},{"emoji":"🎬","c1":"#facc15","c2":"#f87171","title":"Silent Films to Talkies","fact":"Early movies had no recorded sound at all, so they were called silent films. Actors used big movements and expressions to tell the story. In the late 1920s, movies with sound became possible, known as 'talkies'. This was a huge change for the movie industry. Some silent film actors had trouble adjusting to speaking roles. Today, sound is one of the most important parts of any movie."},{"emoji":"🐋","c1":"#06b6d4","c2":"#38bdf8","title":"Shark Teeth","fact":"Sharks can lose thousands of teeth in their life and grow new ones. Their teeth are always being replaced, one row after another. Sharks have been in the ocean for hundreds of millions of years. Most sharks are not dangerous to humans. Sharks are important because they help keep the ocean healthy. Without sharks, other sea animal populations could grow too large."},{"emoji":"🏛️","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#b45309","title":"The Library of Alexandria","fact":"The Library of Alexandria was one of the largest libraries in the ancient world. It was located in Egypt and held thousands of scrolls. Scholars from many countries traveled there to study and learn. The library collected knowledge about science, medicine, and history. Sadly, much of the library was lost over time. It remains a symbol of the importance of knowledge and learning."},{"emoji":"🫀","c1":"#ec4899","c2":"#f472b6","title":"Taste Buds","fact":"You have about 10,000 taste buds on your tongue. They help you taste sweet, sour, salty, bitter, and savory flavors. Taste buds are replaced every couple of weeks. Your sense of smell also affects how food tastes. This is why food can taste different when you have a cold. Trying new foods can help you enjoy more flavors."},{"emoji":"🤖","c1":"#22d3ee","c2":"#6366f1","title":"What Is Coding","fact":"Coding means writing instructions that a computer can understand and follow. These instructions are written in special languages, like Python or JavaScript. Coding is used to make websites, apps, games, and much more. Many schools now teach basic coding to students. Learning to code can help you solve problems in creative ways. Coding is an important skill in today's world."},{"emoji":"🌍","c1":"#22c55e","c2":"#4ade80","title":"Highest Waterfall","fact":"Angel Falls, in Venezuela, is the tallest waterfall in the world. The water falls from a very high, flat mountain called a tepui. It is so tall that some of the water turns into mist before reaching the ground. Angel Falls is located inside a national park in the rainforest. It is named after a pilot who flew over it many years ago. Many travelers visit it to see its incredible height."},{"emoji":"🎨","c1":"#fb7185","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"The Color Wheel","fact":"The color wheel shows how colors relate to each other. Red, blue, and yellow are called primary colors because they cannot be made by mixing other colors. Mixing primary colors creates new colors, like green, orange, and purple. Artists use the color wheel to choose colors that look good together. Understanding color helps artists create different moods in their work. The color wheel is a helpful tool for painters, designers, and students."},{"emoji":"💡","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"The Wheel","fact":"The wheel is one of the oldest and most important inventions. It was invented thousands of years ago. Wheels made it much easier to move heavy things from place to place. They are used in cars, bicycles, and many machines today. Without the wheel, transportation would look very different. Simple inventions like this can change the whole world."},{"emoji":"🔢","c1":"#4ade80","c2":"#60a5fa","title":"Symmetry Everywhere","fact":"Symmetry means that one half of something matches the other half. You can find symmetry in nature, art, and buildings. Butterflies, snowflakes, and flowers often show beautiful symmetry. Artists and architects use symmetry to make designs look balanced and pleasing. Mathematicians study symmetry to understand shapes and patterns. Symmetry connects math, art, and the natural world in an amazing way."},{"emoji":"🍎","c1":"#ef4444","c2":"#f87171","title":"Pizza History","fact":"Pizza started in Naples, Italy, hundreds of years ago. At first, it was a simple, affordable food for working families. Tomatoes were added to pizza after they arrived from the Americas. Pizza became very popular around the world in the last century. Today, there are many different styles of pizza. Almost every country has its own special way of making it."},{"emoji":"⛈️","c1":"#38bdf8","c2":"#7dd3fc","title":"Thunder Sound","fact":"Thunder happens because lightning heats the air very fast. This sudden heat makes the air expand quickly, creating a loud sound. Light travels faster than sound, so we see lightning before we hear thunder. You can guess how far away a storm is by counting the seconds between them. Thunderstorms can also bring strong winds and heavy rain. It is important to stay safe during storms."},{"emoji":"🌱","c1":"#84cc16","c2":"#a3e635","title":"Tree Oxygen","fact":"One big tree can produce enough oxygen for two people. Trees take in carbon dioxide and release oxygen into the air. This process is called photosynthesis. Forests play a big role in keeping our air clean. Trees also provide homes for many animals and insects. Planting trees is a simple way to help the environment."},{"emoji":"🦁","c1":"#f97316","c2":"#ffd166","title":"Dolphin Names","fact":"Dolphins can call each other with special sounds, like names. Scientists call these sounds 'signature whistles'. Each dolphin has its own unique whistle. Dolphins use these whistles to find friends and family in the ocean. They also use clicks and sounds to find food using echolocation. Dolphins are very social animals and often travel in groups called pods."},{"emoji":"🎵","c1":"#f472b6","c2":"#c084fc","title":"Guitar Strings","fact":"A standard guitar usually has six strings. Each string makes a different note when you play it. Guitarists press the strings against the neck to change the sound. Guitars can be acoustic, which means they don't need electricity, or electric, which uses an amplifier. The guitar is one of the most popular instruments in the world. It is used in many types of music, like rock, pop, and folk."},{"emoji":"🚀","c1":"#7c3aed","c2":"#22d3ee","title":"Space Silence","fact":"There is no sound in space because there is no air. Sound needs something to travel through, like air or water. This means astronauts cannot hear explosions or engines outside their spacecraft. They talk to each other using radios instead. Space is also extremely cold and mostly empty. It is one of the strangest and quietest places we know."},{"emoji":"🎬","c1":"#facc15","c2":"#f87171","title":"24 Frames a Second","fact":"Most movies show 24 individual pictures every single second. Each picture is called a frame. Your brain blends these frames together, so it looks like smooth motion. This trick is similar to how cartoons work. Without this illusion, movies would look like a slideshow instead of real movement. Filmmakers have used this idea for over a hundred years."},{"emoji":"🐋","c1":"#06b6d4","c2":"#38bdf8","title":"Sea Otter Hands","fact":"Sea otters hold hands while they sleep so they don't float apart. Groups of sea otters resting together are called 'rafts'. Sea otters also wrap themselves in seaweed to stay in one place. They use rocks as tools to open shellfish for food. Sea otters have very thick fur to stay warm in cold water. They spend most of their lives in the ocean."},{"emoji":"🏛️","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#b45309","title":"Viking Sailors","fact":"The Vikings were skilled sailors from Scandinavia over 1,000 years ago. They built strong wooden ships that could cross rough oceans. Vikings traveled far from home to trade, explore, and settle new lands. Some Vikings reached North America long before other European explorers. They were also skilled craftspeople and storytellers. Many Viking stories and myths are still told today."},{"emoji":"🫀","c1":"#ec4899","c2":"#f472b6","title":"Fingerprints","fact":"No two people in the world have the same fingerprints. Not even identical twins have the same pattern. Fingerprints form before a baby is even born. They help people grip objects better. Police sometimes use fingerprints to identify people. Your fingerprints stay the same your whole life."},{"emoji":"🤖","c1":"#22d3ee","c2":"#6366f1","title":"Artificial Intelligence","fact":"Artificial intelligence, or AI, is when computers learn to complete tasks that normally need human thinking. AI can recognize pictures, understand language, and even play games. It learns by studying huge amounts of information. AI is used in many places, like phones, cars, and websites. Scientists are still working to make AI smarter and safer. AI is one of the fastest-growing areas of technology today."},{"emoji":"🌍","c1":"#22c55e","c2":"#4ade80","title":"Seven Continents","fact":"There are seven continents on Earth. They are Africa, Antarctica, Asia, Australia, Europe, North America, and South America. Each continent has its own unique animals, plants, and cultures. Asia is the largest continent by both size and population. Australia is the smallest continent, but also a whole country. Learning about continents helps us understand our world better."},{"emoji":"🎨","c1":"#fb7185","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"Museums Around the World","fact":"Museums are special places that collect, protect, and display art and history. Some museums focus on paintings, while others show sculptures, science, or ancient artifacts. The largest museums can have millions of visitors every year. Many museums let people see rare and valuable objects up close. Museums help people learn about different cultures and time periods. Visiting a museum is a fun way to explore art and history."},{"emoji":"💡","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"Velcro Idea","fact":"Velcro was invented after a man studied how seeds stick to clothes. He noticed tiny hooks on the seeds that grabbed onto fabric. This gave him the idea to create a new type of fastener. Velcro is now used in clothes, shoes, and even space suits. It is a great example of getting ideas from nature. This process is sometimes called biomimicry."},{"emoji":"🔢","c1":"#4ade80","c2":"#60a5fa","title":"The Only Even Prime","fact":"A prime number can only be divided evenly by 1 and itself. The number 2 is special because it is the only even prime number. Every other even number can be divided by 2, so it cannot be prime. Prime numbers are important in math and even in computer security. Mathematicians have searched for centuries to find bigger and bigger prime numbers. Prime numbers are considered some of the building blocks of mathematics."},{"emoji":"🍎","c1":"#ef4444","c2":"#f87171","title":"Tomato Fruit","fact":"A tomato is a fruit, but we usually cook it like a vegetable. This is because of how it is used in cooking, not how it grows. Tomatoes come in many colors, sizes, and shapes. They are an important ingredient in many dishes, like pasta and salads. Tomatoes are also full of vitamins. They originally came from South America."},{"emoji":"⛈️","c1":"#38bdf8","c2":"#7dd3fc","title":"The Ice Age","fact":"During the Ice Age, much of the Earth was covered in ice. This happened thousands of years ago. Huge sheets of ice, called glaciers, covered large parts of the land. Many animals, like woolly mammoths, lived during this cold time. Scientists study ice and rocks to learn about the Ice Age. Earth's climate has changed many times throughout history."},{"emoji":"🌱","c1":"#84cc16","c2":"#a3e635","title":"Cactus Water","fact":"Cactus plants can store water for a very long time. This helps them survive in hot, dry deserts. Their thick stems hold water like a sponge. Cactus spines help protect them from animals and also reduce water loss. Some cactus plants can live for over 100 years. There are many different types of cactus around the world."},{"emoji":"🦁","c1":"#f97316","c2":"#ffd166","title":"Owl Necks","fact":"Owls can turn their heads almost all the way around. They can rotate their necks about 270 degrees. Owls have this ability because their eyes cannot move much in their sockets. Turning their heads helps them see in almost every direction. Owls also have amazing hearing, which helps them hunt at night. Their soft feathers let them fly without making much noise."},{"emoji":"🎵","c1":"#f472b6","c2":"#c084fc","title":"National Anthems","fact":"Almost every country in the world has its own national anthem. An anthem is a special song that represents a country's history and pride. People often sing anthems at sports events and national holidays. Anthems can be slow and calm, or fast and powerful. Many anthems were written hundreds of years ago. Learning about anthems is a fun way to learn about different cultures."},{"emoji":"🚀","c1":"#7c3aed","c2":"#22d3ee","title":"Milky Way","fact":"Our galaxy is called the Milky Way, and it has billions of stars. Our solar system is just a tiny part of it. The Milky Way is shaped like a big spiral, similar to a pinwheel. It takes our Sun about 230 million years to travel around the galaxy once. On a very dark night, you can see part of the Milky Way as a bright band in the sky. Scientists believe there are billions of other galaxies in the universe."},{"emoji":"🎬","c1":"#facc15","c2":"#f87171","title":"Movie Subtitles","fact":"Subtitles are the written words shown at the bottom of a movie screen. They translate what characters are saying into another language. Subtitles help people enjoy movies from other countries. They can also help people who are deaf or hard of hearing. Watching movies with subtitles is a great way to practice a new language. Many students use subtitles to help them learn English."},{"emoji":"🐋","c1":"#06b6d4","c2":"#38bdf8","title":"Giant Squid Eyes","fact":"The giant squid has the biggest eyes in the animal world. Its eyes can be as big as a basketball. These huge eyes help the giant squid see in the dark, deep ocean. Giant squids live very deep in the water, so people rarely see them. They can grow to be extremely long. Scientists are still learning many things about how giant squids live."},{"emoji":"🏛️","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#b45309","title":"Ancient Rome's Roads","fact":"Ancient Romans built an enormous network of roads across their empire. These roads helped soldiers, traders, and messages travel quickly. Many Roman roads were built so well that parts still exist today. Romans also built amazing aqueducts to carry water into cities. Their engineering skills influenced builders for centuries afterward. The phrase 'all roads lead to Rome' comes from this huge road system."},{"emoji":"🫀","c1":"#ec4899","c2":"#f472b6","title":"Yawning","fact":"Yawning can help cool down your brain. It also brings more oxygen into your body. Yawning is contagious — seeing someone yawn can make you yawn too! People usually yawn when they are tired or bored. Even babies yawn before they are born. Scientists are still studying exactly why we yawn."},{"emoji":"🤖","c1":"#22d3ee","c2":"#6366f1","title":"QR Codes","fact":"A QR code is a square pattern that stores information, like a website link. You can scan it using a smartphone camera. QR codes were first created in Japan to track car parts. Today, they are used on menus, posters, and packages around the world. Scanning a QR code is fast and does not need typing. They are a simple way to share information quickly."},{"emoji":"🌍","c1":"#22c55e","c2":"#4ade80","title":"Dead Sea Floating","fact":"You can float easily in the Dead Sea because the water is very salty. The high salt makes the water denser, so bodies float more easily. The Dead Sea is located between Israel and Jordan. It is actually a lake, not a real sea. Very few living things can survive in its salty water. Many people visit to float and relax in its unique water."},{"emoji":"🎨","c1":"#fb7185","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"Origami Paper Folding","fact":"Origami is the traditional Japanese art of folding paper into shapes. No cutting or gluing is used, only careful folding. Simple origami can make shapes like boats or hats. More advanced origami can create detailed animals or flowers. Origami teaches patience, geometry, and creativity. Today, people all over the world enjoy origami as a relaxing hobby."},{"emoji":"💡","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"The Zipper","fact":"The zipper took many years and many tries to become popular. Early versions did not always work very well. Eventually, a better design made zippers strong and reliable. Zippers became very popular for clothes, bags, and boots. They are much faster to use than buttons. Today, zippers are found in almost every home."},{"emoji":"🔢","c1":"#4ade80","c2":"#60a5fa","title":"The Abacus","fact":"The abacus is one of the earliest tools used for counting and calculating. It uses beads that slide along rods to represent numbers. People in ancient China, Rome, and other cultures used different versions of the abacus. Skilled users can add and subtract very quickly with it. Even today, some people use the abacus to practice mental math. It shows that useful math tools existed long before calculators."},{"emoji":"🍎","c1":"#ef4444","c2":"#f87171","title":"Old Popcorn","fact":"People have eaten popcorn for thousands of years. Ancient corn kernels have even been found that could still pop. Popcorn pops because of the water inside each kernel. When heated, the water turns to steam and makes the kernel explode. Popcorn is a popular snack, especially at movies. It is also a whole grain and can be a healthy snack."},{"emoji":"🦁","c1":"#f97316","c2":"#ffd166","title":"Kangaroo Jumps","fact":"Kangaroos cannot walk backward. Their strong back legs and big tail are made for jumping forward. A kangaroo can jump more than three meters in one hop. Their tail helps them balance while jumping and even while standing still. Baby kangaroos, called joeys, live in their mother's pouch. Kangaroos are found mostly in Australia."},{"emoji":"🎵","c1":"#f472b6","c2":"#c084fc","title":"Whistling as Music","fact":"Whistling is one of the oldest ways humans have made music. You don't need any instrument at all, just your mouth! Some people can whistle entire songs with amazing detail. In some cultures, whistled languages are even used to communicate across mountains. Birds also use whistling sounds to communicate with each other. Whistling shows that music can be made almost anywhere, anytime."},{"emoji":"🚀","c1":"#7c3aed","c2":"#22d3ee","title":"Jupiter Storm","fact":"Jupiter has a giant storm bigger than Earth called the Great Red Spot. This storm has been happening for hundreds of years. Jupiter is the biggest planet in our solar system. It is made mostly of gas, with no solid surface to stand on. Jupiter also has more than 90 moons. Its strong gravity helps protect Earth by pulling in some space rocks."},{"emoji":"🎬","c1":"#facc15","c2":"#f87171","title":"Stunt Doubles","fact":"Stunt doubles are trained performers who do dangerous scenes instead of the main actors. This keeps actors safe during jumps, falls, or car chases. Stunt performers train for years to do these actions safely. They often wear hidden safety equipment during filming. Some stunts still require months of practice to get right. Their work makes action movies exciting and believable."},{"emoji":"🐋","c1":"#06b6d4","c2":"#38bdf8","title":"Turtle Journeys","fact":"Sea turtles can swim thousands of kilometers to lay their eggs. Many turtles return to the exact same beach where they were born. Baby sea turtles hatch from eggs buried in the sand. They then crawl to the ocean, often at night. Sea turtles can live for many decades. Some species of sea turtles are endangered and need our protection."},{"emoji":"🏛️","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#b45309","title":"The Terracotta Army","fact":"The Terracotta Army is a collection of thousands of clay soldier statues in China. It was built to protect the tomb of China's first emperor. Each statue has a different face and expression. The statues were buried underground for over 2,000 years before being discovered. Archaeologists are still studying the site today. It is considered one of the greatest archaeological discoveries in history."},{"emoji":"🫀","c1":"#ec4899","c2":"#f472b6","title":"Sleep Time","fact":"Most people spend about one third of their life sleeping. Sleep helps your body and brain rest and repair. Children usually need more sleep than adults. While you sleep, your brain organizes memories from the day. Not getting enough sleep can make it hard to think clearly. Having a regular sleep schedule can help you feel more energetic."},{"emoji":"🤖","c1":"#22d3ee","c2":"#6366f1","title":"Satellites in Space","fact":"Satellites are machines that orbit the Earth in space. They help with things like weather forecasts, TV signals, and GPS navigation. The first satellite, called Sputnik, was launched in 1957. Today, thousands of satellites circle our planet. Satellites allow people to communicate across huge distances instantly. They play an important role in our daily lives, even if we don't see them."},{"emoji":"🌍","c1":"#22c55e","c2":"#4ade80","title":"Time Zones","fact":"The Earth is divided into 24 time zones. This helps different parts of the world keep time based on the position of the Sun. When it is morning in one country, it can be night in another. Time zones were created to help with travel and communication. Some very large countries have several time zones. Understanding time zones is important when talking to people around the world."},{"emoji":"🎨","c1":"#fb7185","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"Mosaic Art","fact":"A mosaic is a picture or pattern made from many small pieces of colored material. These pieces can be glass, stone, or tile. Ancient civilizations used mosaics to decorate floors and walls. Making a mosaic takes patience, since every small piece must be placed carefully. Mosaics can last for thousands of years without fading. Some ancient mosaics are still beautiful today."},{"emoji":"💡","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"First Chocolate Bar","fact":"The first chocolate bar was made in the 1800s. Before that, chocolate was mostly a drink, not something solid to eat. New machines made it possible to turn chocolate into smooth, solid bars. Chocolate quickly became a popular treat around the world. Today, there are many different types and flavors of chocolate. It remains one of the most loved foods worldwide."},{"emoji":"🔢","c1":"#4ade80","c2":"#60a5fa","title":"Hexagons in Nature","fact":"A hexagon is a shape with six equal sides. Bees build their honeycombs using hexagons because this shape uses the least amount of wax while holding the most honey. This makes the hive strong and efficient. Hexagons are also found in snowflakes and certain rock formations. Mathematicians admire hexagons for being both simple and extremely efficient. Nature often finds the smartest mathematical solutions on its own."},{"emoji":"🍎","c1":"#ef4444","c2":"#f87171","title":"Tea Popularity","fact":"Tea is one of the most popular drinks in the world, after water. It has been enjoyed for thousands of years, especially in Asia. Tea comes from the leaves of a plant called Camellia sinensis. There are many types of tea, like green, black, and herbal tea. Different countries have their own special ways of making tea. Drinking tea is also a way people relax and spend time together."},{"emoji":"🦁","c1":"#f97316","c2":"#ffd166","title":"Whale Songs","fact":"Whales sing songs that can travel for many kilometers under the water. Male humpback whales are famous for their long, beautiful songs. Scientists think whales sing to talk to other whales or to find a partner. Whale songs can change slowly over many years. Whales are also some of the biggest animals on Earth. They breathe air, just like humans, even though they live in water."},{"emoji":"🎵","c1":"#f472b6","c2":"#c084fc","title":"Music Without Words","fact":"Instrumental music has no singing, only instruments. It can still tell a story or create a feeling. Movie soundtracks are a great example of instrumental music. Composers choose notes carefully to make you feel happy, scared, or excited. Music without words is understood by people who speak different languages. This is one reason why music is sometimes called a universal language."},{"emoji":"🚀","c1":"#7c3aed","c2":"#22d3ee","title":"Shooting Stars","fact":"A shooting star is not a star — it is a small rock burning in the sky. These rocks are called meteors, and they come from space. When a meteor enters Earth's atmosphere, it burns up and creates a bright streak of light. Most meteors are very small, about the size of a grain of sand. Sometimes many meteors appear together, called a meteor shower. People often make a wish when they see one!"},{"emoji":"🎬","c1":"#facc15","c2":"#f87171","title":"3D Movies","fact":"3D movies use special glasses to make images look like they pop out of the screen. Each eye sees a slightly different image through the glasses. Your brain combines both images to create the feeling of depth. This trick makes objects look closer or farther away than they really are. 3D technology has been used in movies since the 1950s. It is still popular in theaters today."},{"emoji":"🏛️","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#b45309","title":"Machu Picchu","fact":"Machu Picchu is an ancient Inca city high in the mountains of Peru. It was built without using wheels or modern tools. The stones fit together so perfectly that no mortar was needed. For centuries, it stayed hidden from the outside world. Today, it is one of the most famous historical sites on Earth. Visitors travel from all over the world to see its incredible views."},{"emoji":"🤖","c1":"#22d3ee","c2":"#6366f1","title":"3D Printing","fact":"A 3D printer builds real objects layer by layer, using melted material. It can create toys, tools, and even parts for machines. Some 3D printers use plastic, while others can use metal or other materials. 3D printing is used in medicine, engineering, and art. It allows people to design and build their own creations. This technology is becoming more common in schools and homes."},{"emoji":"🎨","c1":"#fb7185","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"Street Art and Murals","fact":"Murals are large paintings created on walls, often in public places. Street art can turn plain city walls into colorful works of art. Some murals tell a story or celebrate local culture and history. Artists use special techniques to make murals last outdoors for years. Many cities now support street art as a way to brighten public spaces. Murals allow art to be enjoyed by everyone, not just in museums."},{"emoji":"🔢","c1":"#4ade80","c2":"#60a5fa","title":"Really Big Numbers","fact":"A googol is a huge number written as a 1 followed by 100 zeros. It is much larger than the number of stars in the observable universe. Mathematicians created googol just to explore the idea of extremely large numbers. The name of the company Google was actually inspired by this number. Big numbers like this help scientists describe huge amounts, like distances in space. Exploring huge numbers is a fun way to imagine the size of the universe."},{"emoji":"🦁","c1":"#f97316","c2":"#ffd166","title":"Tiger Stripes","fact":"No two tigers have the same pattern of stripes. Just like human fingerprints, each tiger's stripes are unique. Tiger stripes also grow on their skin, not only on their fur. This means if you shaved a tiger, it would still have stripes! Tigers are excellent swimmers, unlike most cats. They are also the largest wild cats in the world."},{"emoji":"🎵","c1":"#f472b6","c2":"#c084fc","title":"The Xylophone","fact":"A xylophone is a percussion instrument made of wooden bars. Each bar makes a different note when you hit it with a mallet. Similar instruments have been used in Africa and Asia for centuries. The word 'xylophone' comes from Greek words meaning 'wood' and 'sound'. Xylophones are often used to teach children about music. They are colorful, fun, and easy to start playing."},{"emoji":"🚀","c1":"#7c3aed","c2":"#22d3ee","title":"Space Suits","fact":"A space suit protects astronauts and lets them breathe in space. It gives them oxygen and keeps their body at a safe temperature. Space suits are also very heavy, but they feel lighter in space because of low gravity. They protect astronauts from dangerous space rocks and strong sunlight. Putting on a full space suit can take a long time. Astronauts practice wearing their suits before every spacewalk."},{"emoji":"🎬","c1":"#facc15","c2":"#f87171","title":"Movie Music Scores","fact":"A movie score is the music written specifically for a film. Composers create music to match the emotions of each scene. Exciting scenes often have fast, loud music, while sad scenes use slow, quiet music. A great movie score can make a scene feel even more powerful. Some movie music becomes famous even outside of the film. Film composers work closely with directors to tell the story through sound."},{"emoji":"🏛️","c1":"#eab308","c2":"#b45309","title":"Ancient Writing Systems","fact":"Some of the earliest writing systems were created thousands of years ago. Ancient Egyptians used pictures called hieroglyphics to write. Ancient Mesopotamians used a system called cuneiform, pressed into clay. Writing allowed people to record history, laws, and stories. Before writing, information was passed down only by speaking. The invention of writing changed how humans shared knowledge forever."},{"emoji":"🤖","c1":"#22d3ee","c2":"#6366f1","title":"Early Computers","fact":"The first computers were as big as an entire room. They were much slower than the small computers we use today. Early computers used large tubes and switches instead of tiny chips. Over the years, computers became smaller, faster, and much more powerful. Today, a simple smartphone can do more than those first giant computers. Technology continues to change at an amazing speed."},{"emoji":"🎨","c1":"#fb7185","c2":"#fbbf24","title":"Self-Portraits","fact":"A self-portrait is when an artist paints or draws a picture of themselves. Many famous painters throughout history created self-portraits. Self-portraits can show how an artist sees themselves or wants to be seen. They were especially useful before cameras were invented. Today, some people compare self-portraits to modern photographs, like selfies. Self-portraits give us a personal look into an artist's life."},{"emoji":"🔢","c1":"#4ade80","c2":"#60a5fa","title":"Math and Music","fact":"Music and math are closely connected. Rhythm is based on counting beats and dividing time into equal parts. Musical scales are built using mathematical patterns between notes. Composers sometimes use number patterns to create melodies. Even musical instruments, like a guitar or piano, are built using precise mathematical measurements. This connection shows how math can be found in creative and artistic places too."}];
